{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJtL9bZ9HeqUtsQXYwJL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YXdNTgvRRi2RhFesVVTK83","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"cases":[{"id":"audience_protected","met":true,"report_quote":"audience containing the exact `RESOURCE`. Missing claims raise `KeyError`, so they fail closed.","reason":"F5 correctly cites gateway.py lines 10-22 and 20 as enforcing the exact RESOURCE audience. It makes no audience-bypass allegation. It treats the SDK audience advisories as applicable only if an SDK verifier is used."},{"id":"cache_protected","met":true,"report_quote":"The key includes tenant, subject, policy version and tool set, and `authenticate` (including revocation) runs before any cache hit. I traced no cross-tenant or cross-user hit and no stale-grant hit (`likely_pass`, static reasoning only).","reason":"The report recognises the full cache key and alleges no cross-tenant hit. Its F2 gap is about missing TTL, size cap and invalidation. Those are real source-local properties of lines 37-40, and dispatch never touches CACHE."},{"id":"batch_protected","met":true,"report_quote":"Every batch element passes through `invoke`, so there is no per-element bypass. Sequential execution with earlier effects surviving a later denial (lines 32-33) is not a violation, because no atomicity contract is stated.","reason":"F6 makes no batch bypass claim and asserts no gap. It also does not treat sequential execution as a violation."},{"id":"stop_protected","met":true,"report_quote":"It stops only on cancel, subject revocation or token expiry.","reason":"The report describes the worker_step stop checks at line 50. It states that stop time, multi-replica propagation and process-local REVOKED are unknown, and claims no measured fleet effectiveness. The frozen-claims point is labelled needs_evidence (potential gap) and not a confirmed gap, which is a reasonable reading of line 52."},{"